	Nspec + Vgl  	go to the fields..hw 	y\a÷-qø qay vepos 	Nspec + Vgl  	walk along a roadnote	cf. Mand. z«o , Thai d˙˙n thaa≥..hw 	qay p˙ vepos 	Vh + Vvgl  	send off; *dispatch (on an errand, mission, etc.)..hw 	qay p˙ p»î vepos 	Vh + Vv + Vvgl  	send off; dispatch (on an errand, mission, etc.) (3rd. person obj.)..hw 	qay-v»ï vepos 	Vgl  	go a long way; be a long way to go..hw 	qay m»a v»ïpos 	VPgl  	not be far to go..hw 	qay-qay l\a-l\a te vepos 	AE + Vgl  	go back and forth; keep going and comingngl 	2. be going (of a situation); be in/go a certain way; be like (of an object)note	cf. Eng. How does that song go?ex  	chi t»e qh»a÷ —ø \ø-lø-\ø-qh»a l|ay c\˙ qh\a-qhe qay ve le exgl	How is everything going in this village?ex  	qh\a-qhe qay l‰-n—a q»o÷-ma, c\a÷-p\o chi qhe ve m‰ exgl	I wonder what it would be like--an airplane like that!xx  	     AEstat + qay  (AE + V)        be AEstat; become AEstat; get to be AEstatnote	used as a supporting verb for preceding AEstat's; cf. AEstat + te, AEstat + ph\‰÷..hw 	q\ø÷ \‰ qay vepos 	AEstat + Vgl  	get crooked..hw 	th»e \‰ qay vepos 	AEstat + Vgl  	straighten..hw 	n|î \‰ qay vepos 	AEstat + Vgl  	get red, reddenex  	n\ø qh»‰ n|î \‰ qay ve l»a exgl	Have your stools become red? ("Are your stools going redly?")ngl 	3. end up in a certain way; turn out; come to pass thus; eventuateex  	n»o h|a-ph»ø k˙ a l»a qo —ø ≥\a l\‰ n»‰÷-k\a÷ qay y\o exgl	If I should fall up there among the rocks, I'd end up in smithereens...hw 	qay-g\a e vepos 	V + Pvgl  	reach a certain placenote	usually pronounced with vocalic fusion as qay ge veex  	«s|ø-p—ø qay-g\a t\u d»ø —a ve exgl	We've planned to reach there in the morning...hw 	qay-g\e÷ e vepos 	[V + Bv] + Pvgl  	a. turn out a certain wayngl 	b. go off somewherenote	g\e÷ (Bv) [q.v.] is a bound morpheme conveying a nuance of vividness after certain verbs of motion; it is always followed by e (Pv) 'transitive motion' [q.v.]; g\e÷ arose as a fusion of g\a (V) 'arrive' + e (Pv) [qq.v.]; after the fusion a 'new' e could then be added (g\e e); the glottal stop seems to have arisen epenthetically to separate the two like vowels [g\e-÷-e]; a semantically less specialized fusion of g\a + e occurs in qay-g\a e ve (V + Pv) [previous entry]..hw 	chi hï-hï qay-g\e÷ e vepos 	Next + VPgl  	turn out too big..hw 	chi-h|ï|‰ qay-g\e÷ e vepos 	Next + VPgl  	turn out too small..hw 	c»ø-l\ø÷ \‰ qay-g\e÷ e vepos 	AEstat + VPgl  	turn out perfectly; come out just rightex  	|a-p\o÷ chi c»ø-l\ø÷ \‰ qay-g\e÷ e exgl	This shirt turned out perfect!ex  	t»e k\a qay-g\e÷ e exgl	He's gone off someplace..hw 	qaypos 	Vvgl  	1. go and Vhnote	cf. ca (vV); cf. the Si. aux. verb paj, some of whose usages parallel those of qay (Vv)ex  	«s|ø —ø l\‰ Ÿg\˙÷ qay y\o h|‰ exgl	I'll probably go and harvest in the morning.ex  	c»o ph»ø ca l—e-g»ï qay-÷ exgl	Go and play over there!note	as in this ex., ca and qay often co-occur in the same VP, flanking the Vhngl 	2. Vh along; Vh away from..hw 	j»u qay vepos 	Vh + Vvgl  	walk along..hw 	m|‰ qay vepos 	Vh + Vvgl  	disappear..hw 	«s—î qay vepos 	Vh + Vvgl  	lead smn along..hw 	«s—î-qay-«s‰-qaypos 	Elabvgl  	lead smn along ..hw 	y\u qay vepos 	Vh + Vvgl  	take awaynote	SYN. y\u e ve (V + Pv)ngl 	3. go on Vh'ing; keep on Vh'ingnote	cf. ch»‰ (Vv)ex  	te qay «s—e -- t»a j»‰ exgl	Keep on doing it--don't stop!..hw 	Ÿga q\ø÷ ti qay vepos 	vV + vV + Vh + Vvgl  	have to keep on replantingex  	l‰, Ÿga q\ø÷ ti qay ve \ø-y»an \ø-qhø lo qo, m»a t»a exgl	Besides, if it's during the time I have to keep on transplanting, I won't have time...hw 	«s—a-b»ø÷=p—a t»e chi Ÿg»a ve \ø-qhø lo y»a-c\o=«si f|ï-k»o÷-ni t»e Ÿg»a y»ø «su c\e te qay xx  	     «s—a-b»ø÷=p—a t»e chi Ÿg»a ve \ø-qhø lo y»a-c\o=«si f|ï-k»o÷-ni t»e Ÿg»a y»ø «su c\e te qay ex  	ve c»e exgl	Among these ten hunters was a certain orphaned parentless fellow xx  	              who used to act as servant to the o